<blockquote class="uncited"><div>OK... I haven't really played around with the DMR part of my TYT MD-UV380<br>since I put the Opengd77 firmware into it. Today... I decided to play around<br>with it some.<br><br>I seen for the DMR ID list... it could be downloaded from  RadioID.net or<br>HamDigital or you could specify a URL. I tried to download the DMR ID but<br>I was only getting under 5,000 DMR IDs. When I see the "Region" was set to<br>312 (by default)... I deleted that and left that field blank  and then I was<br>able to download I guess full DMR ID list (280,000+). <br><br>Well... I only wanted the USA and Canada... so I went to a different site<br>where I was able to download the the USA and Canada. I told the site<br>that I was downloading it for use on the TYR MD-380/390. I downloaded<br>a .CSV file with 131,000+ DRM IDs.<br><br>I then imported this .CSV file into the Opengd77 software and wrote it<br>to the radio. When receiving a DMR transmission... it was only showing<br>me the callsign of the DMR station. The .CSV file I have has First name,<br>Country, City and State in it.<br><br>Now... is there a reason for nothing else getting displayed when I receive<br>a DMR transmission??? Is a downloaded file for the TYT MD-380/390 not<br>going to work properly with the Opengd77 software??? If so... then how<br>would I setup the Opengd77 software to only download DMR IDs for just<br>the USA and Canada???<br><br>Also... I see a setting in the Opengd77 software that says... "Data record<br>length"... the default is 16 characters. I tried setting this to 50 in hopes<br>it would display Callsign, Name, City, State, and Country... but still only<br>get the callsign displayed. I noticed that changing the number of characters<br>changes how many DMR IDs can be written to the radio.<br><br>So... I would really like to know if there is a way to get the radio to<br>show the Callsign, Name, City, State, and Country of  the DMR station<br>that I'm receiving... or will it only show the callsign<br><br>Thanks,<br><br>Mike - N1EVH</div></blockquote>Everything you're asking is in the OpenGD77 reference manual.<br><a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... r_Guide.md</a><br><br>EA3V  73<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4014">EA3V</a> — Fri Apr 04, 2025 11:05 pm</p><hr />
